{"primaryContentSections":[{"declarations":[{"platforms":["macOS"],"languages":["swift"],"tokens":[{"text":"@","kind":"attribute"},{"preciseIdentifier":"s:ScM","text":"MainActor","kind":"attribute"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"struct","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"OUDSToolBarTop","kind":"identifier"}]}],"kind":"declarations"},{"content":[{"type":"heading","anchor":"overview","text":"Overview","level":2},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"strong","inlineContent":[{"text":"Warning","type":"text"}]},{"text":": If an item is placed in principal position, the subtitle is never displayed (whatever ","type":"text"},{"code":"hasLargeTitle","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" is), because","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"SwiftUI’s ","type":"text"},{"code":".principal","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" placement only replaces the inline compact bar title, not ","type":"text"},{"code":".navigationSubtitle()","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" (iOS 26+), which would","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"otherwise keep rendering next to the item with no visible title next to it. The title itself is displayed only if ","type":"text"},{"code":"hasLargeTitle","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"is ","type":"text"},{"code":"true","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" (in that case it appears below the bar, in large title mode, not inside it).","type":"text"}]},{"type":"heading","anchor":"Appearances","text":"Appearances","level":2},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"With Liquid Glass \/ iOS 26+ the OS will change the rendering of the toolbar items depending to the context:","type":"text"}]},{"type":"unorderedList","items":[{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"The OS can group the items of same types in one group with kind of rectangle (e.g. views with menus)"}],"type":"paragraph"}]},{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"But for buttons items they will remain isolated"}],"type":"paragraph"}]},{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"The placement of the title can be leading or centered depending to the length of the text"}],"type":"paragraph"}]},{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"The text can be truncated if there is not enough remaining space"}],"type":"paragraph"}]},{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"The OS can apply another style for the back button"}],"type":"paragraph"}]}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"Without Liquid Glass \/ iOS 18 and lower, the OS won’t change that much the style of the toolbar items, Items won’t be visually grouped.","type":"text"}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"Globaly the appearence of the * navigation bar* elements is changed by the ","type":"text"},{"code":"oudsNavigationBarAppearance","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"helper of ","type":"text"},{"code":"View","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" that must be applyed on the root view of the ","type":"text"},{"code":"NavigationStack","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" for example.","type":"text"}]},{"type":"heading","anchor":"Technical-constraints","text":"Technical constraints","level":2},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"To be sure for iOS 18 and lower the back buttton and text have the good color, in your main view apply the following accent color:","type":"text"}]},{"type":"codeListing","syntax":"swift","code":["    struct AppMainView: View {","        var body: some View {","            ContentView()","                .accentColor(theme.colors.contentDefault)","        }","    }"]},{"type":"heading","anchor":"Platform-considerations","text":"Platform considerations","level":2},{"type":"unorderedList","items":[{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"text":"The component is available on iOS, iPadOS, and visionOS","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}]},{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"text":"The component is not available for watchOS, tvOS and macOS","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}]}]},{"level":2,"text":"Badges uses","type":"heading","anchor":"Badges-uses"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"For iOS 26 with Liquid Glass, the system badge is used because the OUDS badge component does not provide a suitable","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"rendering with the glassified effect applied on the top toolbar.","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"For iOS until 18 and without Liquid Glass  OUDS badge component is always used.","type":"text"}]},{"level":2,"text":"Code sample","type":"heading","anchor":"Code-sample"},{"type":"codeListing","syntax":"swift","code":["    ContentView()","        .toolBarTop(\"Title\",","            leadingItems: {","                OUDSToolBarItem(navigation: .back())","            },","            principalItem: OUDSToolBarItem(icon: Image(decorative: \"search\"), accessibilityLabel: \"Search\") { \/* Action to process *\/ },","            trailingItems: {","                OUDSToolBarItem(label: \"Label\") { \/* Action to process *\/ }","                OUDSToolBarItem(icon: Image(decorative: \"some_image\"), accessibilityLabel: \"Label\") { \/* Action to process *\/ }","            }","        )"]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"A ","type":"text"},{"code":"View","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" helper can also be used to apply a SwiftUI toolbar configuration."}]},{"code":["    toolBarTop(_:hasLargeTitle:subtitle:leadingItems:principalItem:trailingItems:)"],"type":"codeListing","syntax":"swift"},{"type":"heading","anchor":"Design-documentation","text":"Design documentation","level":2},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"isActive":true,"identifier":"https:\/\/r.orange.fr\/r\/S-ouds-doc-ios-tool-bar-top","type":"reference"}]},{"text":"Themes rendering","anchor":"Themes-rendering","level":2,"type":"heading"},{"text":"Liquid Glass","anchor":"Liquid-Glass","level":3,"type":"heading"},{"type":"heading","anchor":"Orange","text":"O